 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Words about festivals:\n• a festival, a celebration, a ceremony, a ritual, a parade (march-past), a procession, a feast;\n• a masquerade (dancers wearing masks), a traditional dance, a drummer, a choir;\n• costume, regalia (the special clothes and objects of a chief), beads, a headdress;\n• to celebrate, to perform, to commemorate (to remember an event), to honour, to organise;\n• heritage (traditions passed down from the past), custom, tradition, an elder, the palace, the chief (the Fon, the Lamido, the Sultan).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Complete: “The Fon wore his ___ — a beaded hat and a long robe — for the festival.”",
  "steps": [
   "The special clothes and objects of a chief are called regalia.",
   "So the word is “regalia”."
  ],
  "answer": "regalia",
  "checks": []
 },
